#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0127 expect=noViolation domain=SE
#note "POLARITY PIN, silent direction -- the partner of CDISC-SEND-0127-invalid_last_se_ne_dsstdtc-SE. The last Subject Element (SESEQ=2) ends 2020-01-15, EXACTLY the disposition date, which the sheet Rule 'SEENDTC = DS.DSSTDTC of the disposition' names as conformant, so the rule must be silent. Against the pre-M3-D1 == form this file REPORTED the conforming subject; the pair pins the polarity from both sides rather than merely pinning that something fires. NOT vacuous: changing SEENDTC on row 2 to 2020-01-20 makes this same file fire, which is the invalid sibling."
#library standard=sendig version=3-0
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
col SEENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Element"
---
S1 | SE | 001 | 1 | SCRN | 2020-01-01 | 2020-01-10
S1 | SE | 001 | 2 | TRT | 2020-01-10 | 2020-01-15
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | 2020-01-15
---
